worth|monetary-value|ADJECTIVE|having a particular financial value|Having a financial value equal to a stated amount.|trị giá; đáng giá|The signed first edition is worth more than the ordinary copy.|Bản in đầu tiên có chữ ký trị giá cao hơn bản thông thường.|Predicative worth an amount or more than something; normally not used before a noun in this sense.|0
worth|value|NOUN|value of someone or something|The value or importance that someone or something has.|giá trị; tầm quan trọng|The journey showed the worth of careful preparation.|Chuyến đi cho thấy giá trị của việc chuẩn bị kỹ lưỡng.|Usually uncountable; the worth of something or someone's worth. This noun differs from predicative worth doing.|1
worth|deserving-effort|ADJECTIVE|deserving the effort required|Good or useful enough to justify the effort, time, or attention involved.|đáng; đáng bỏ công|The hilltop view is worth the long climb.|Cảnh nhìn từ đỉnh đồi đáng để bỏ công leo lên.|Worth something or worth doing something; not normally worth to do. Used after a linking verb.|2
dramatic|striking-change|ADJECTIVE|striking in size or effect|Large, sudden, or striking enough to attract attention.|mạnh; rõ rệt; gây ấn tượng|The new lighting made a dramatic difference to the hall.|Hệ thống chiếu sáng mới tạo ra sự khác biệt rõ rệt cho hội trường.|Common before change, difference, rise, or fall; the effect may be striking without involving theatre.|0
dramatic|theatre|ADJECTIVE|relating to theatrical performance|Relating to plays or theatrical performance.|thuộc kịch; thuộc sân khấu|The course combines dramatic techniques with voice training.|Khóa học kết hợp kỹ thuật sân khấu với luyện giọng.|Attributive in dramatic art or dramatic techniques; separate from a dramatic change in size or effect.|1
foster|encourage-development|VERB|encourage something to develop|To help a feeling, ability, or activity grow or develop.|nuôi dưỡng; thúc đẩy|Shared projects foster trust between the two classes.|Các dự án chung nuôi dưỡng sự tin tưởng giữa hai lớp.|Transitive foster something; common abstract objects include trust, understanding, and cooperation.|0
foster|temporary-child-care|VERB|care for another person's child|To care for another person's child in your home for a period without becoming the child's adoptive parent.|nhận chăm sóc tạm thời; nuôi dưỡng trẻ theo hình thức chăm sóc thay thế|The couple fostered two siblings while a longer-term home was arranged.|Hai vợ chồng nhận chăm sóc hai anh em trong khi một nơi ở lâu dài hơn được thu xếp.|Transitive foster a child; also intransitive in they foster. Foster care differs from adoption; arrangements vary by place.|1
mission|important-task|NOUN|important task or purpose|An important task or purpose that a person or group is expected to carry out.|nhiệm vụ; sứ mệnh|The rescue team's mission was to find the missing walkers.|Nhiệm vụ của đội cứu hộ là tìm những người đi bộ bị mất tích.|Countable for a particular task; a mission to do something or on a mission. The purpose may also be stated as someone's mission.|0
page|sheet-or-side|NOUN|side of a sheet in a book or document|One side of a sheet of paper in a book or document, or the information printed there.|trang; trang giấy|A handwritten note covered the last page of the diary.|Một ghi chú viết tay phủ kín trang cuối của cuốn nhật ký.|Countable; on page ten for location, turn a page for movement. A leaf can have two pages, one on each side.|0
